{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787865423551683464,"compiled_state":{"alias":"insane-poetic-borer","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5ba5e99f76e98e7d25556f9efd8d6a5abbfeb636e674e0fb78fd1ddc85a85692","event_uuid":"76ad2c97-8cf2-4d97-8561-45af6b55a4e8","position":{"commit_sha":"78f62607b5a383bfea9375033ca47d4a42926b28","position":"1787855605495328001-76ad2c97-8cf2-4d97-8561-45af6b55a4e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9923ce406035ed48611a4b7982f39c3133dc3514c476bed94ecbcdc66e51e103","event_uuid":"eecc542d-5a50-4e47-9dff-f2e3e2285265","position":{"commit_sha":"6684c1855a2ad0f31bf348359a98b9b58b889ed5","position":"1787855633813322001-eecc542d-5a50-4e47-9dff-f2e3e2285265"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3dce82e3be3c853a91bde235d93021fbd7aa8e23a22af5b52331f5459ab5a9a0","event_uuid":"a2906e89-67ae-4154-9441-084a0fafced7","position":{"commit_sha":"787eeed6c397b5d631dbf61bfe25d3816e2fe263","position":"1787855669664200001-a2906e89-67ae-4154-9441-084a0fafced7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787855605495328001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eecc542d-5a50-4e47-9dff-f2e3e2285265","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe sandbox enforcement tests added by `e668-b496-e264-4283` in\n`tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py` assert only that a file is ABSENT after\nrunning a wrapped subprocess:\n\n```python\nassert not target.exists()          # denial \"proven\"\n```\n\nNothing asserts the sandboxed child actually launched and reached the write attempt.\nIf `sandbox-exec`/`bwrap` fails to start at all — bad profile, missing binary, a\nnamespace refusal, an argv regression — the write never happens, the file is absent,\nand the test PASSES. A total failure of the sandbox wrapper is indistinguishable from\ncorrect enforcement.\n\n`test_the_incident_shape_rm_rf_is_denied` has the same shape in reverse: it asserts a\npre-existing `keep.txt` still exists. A sandbox launch failure trivially leaves the file\nin place, producing a false pass.\n\n## Why this matters more than a normal test gap\n\nThese are the ONLY tests that demonstrate the sandbox works. `e668`'s acceptance\ncriteria deliberately required observed enforcement rather than argv assertions,\nprecisely so the control could not be satisfied by construction alone. A test that\npasses when the mechanism is absent silently reintroduces the weakness those criteria\nwere written to exclude — the evidence for the whole feature rests on it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every enforcement test asserts positive LIVENESS of the sandboxed child: the\n      child ran and reached the write attempt (e.g. a sentinel written to an ALLOWED\n      path in the same command, or an asserted exit code / stderr signature that only\n      an executed-and-denied child produces).\n- [ ] The liveness assertion is proven load-bearing: with the sandbox mechanism forced\n      unavailable so the child never launches, the test goes RED rather than green.\n      Demonstrated by real substitution, not asserted.\n- [ ] `test_the_incident_shape_rm_rf_is_denied` gains the same liveness check, so a\n      launch failure cannot pass as \"the target survived\".\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- No enforcement test in the file can pass when the sandbox fails to launch.\n- Each liveness check is shown RED under a forced launch failure.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nFound by the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on change 2256 (patch sets 4 and 7; advisory, so\nit did not block the merge). Discovered from `e668-b496-e264-4283`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"add positive liveness assertions to every enforcement test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c100-c4f1-2a2b-4905","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Sandbox enforcement tests pass when the sandbox fails to launch","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["76ad2c97-8cf2-4d97-8561-45af6b55a4e8","eecc542d-5a50-4e47-9dff-f2e3e2285265","a2906e89-67ae-4154-9441-084a0fafced7"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787865423551683464,"uuid":"ee14d423-9fd5-4643-987b-87edde436f2d"}